<title>UK: Euromarket turnover rose in week to 17 July  -ISMA.</title>
<headline>Euromarket turnover rose in week to 17 July  -ISMA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in the Eurobond and related markets rose to $1.037 trillion in the week to July 17 from $1.019 trillion in the previous week, International Securities Market Association figures show (in billions of dollars).</p>
<p>					    LATEST WEEK	PREVIOUS WEEK</p>
<p> PRIMARY MARKET:			  59.98			62.33</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	 30.61			36.66</p>
<p> SECONDARY MARKET:		     977.09		     957.45</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	264.16		     233.19</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH EUROCLEAR	   737.18		     725.81</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH CEDEL		 299.89		     294.02</p>
<p>--London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
